      "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
      "name": "Divine Destruction",
      "sort": 800000,
      "system": {
        "actionType": {
          "value": "passive"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": "defensive",
        "deathNote": true,
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>When the divine warden is reduced to 0 HP, it erupts with divine energy in a @Template[emanation|distance:30], dealing @Damage[4d6[void]|options:area-damage] damage. Each creature in the area must attempt a @Check[will|dc:18|options:area-effect,damaging-effect] save with the following outcomes.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes full damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and becomes temporarily cursed by the patron deity. The creature becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 1} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for 1 day; this is a curse effect that uses the Will save DC as the counteract DC.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the creature becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 2} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 2}.</p>",
          "gm": ""
        },
